From e6a215383e3e37b3cf08c4492ce9ed368314da1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ronghua Zeng <ronghuaz@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 03:27:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostap: Add WPA2/WPA3 Enterprise (802.1X/EAP) support with
 EAP-TLS fast reauth

Enable full WPA2/WPA3 Enterprise (802.1X/EAP) support on QCC730 with EAP-TLS
fast reauthentication via TLS session resumption (abbreviated handshake).

This implementation targets fullmac drivers where the firmware handles 802.11
authentication, association, and the 4-way handshake, while the host runs only
the EAP state machine.

Key Features:
- Full EAP state machine integration (PEAP, TTLS, EAP-TLS)
- TLS session-ID resumption for fast reauth (abbreviated handshake)
- EAPOL-Start suppression on PMKSA cache-hit
- DH parameter setup guard for mbedtls (client-only)
- Deep-copy EAPOL_RX events to prevent stack overflow in data path
- Pause wpas_periodic()'s 10s eloop timeout while the device is in BMPS,
  so the host does not force a periodic wakeup that is unrelated to any
  real work (root cause of periodic RTOS-timer wakeups out of BMPS on
  QCC730 fullmac builds: EXIT_REASON_RTOS_TIME every ~10s)
- Invalidate the global TLS session cache (used for the fast-reauth
  resumption above) whenever the host detects that EAP credentials for
  an SSID have changed, so a wrong/changed password cannot reconnect by
  resuming a session established under the old credentials and skipping
  the inner EAP method (MSCHAPv2/PAP/CHAP) entirely
---
